{"agent_id":"pp3g-JKN0-implement-146-phase-3-watcher-kill-restart-recovery","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-06T06:25:53.660712367Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"055ac696-f51f-4c63-9498-cf99b79299f3","comment_uuid":"6d3e1871-5a3a-4f14-b304-2bf2052294e7","author":"pp3g-JKN0-implement-146-phase-3-watcher-kill-restart-recovery","content":"Plan: upgrade tools/kickoff-notify.py from Phase 1 (monitor+notify) to Phase 3 (KILL-AND-RESTART) behind an opt-in flag, per the #136/#137 gate criteria.\n\n(1) CONFIG — KICKOFF_RECOVERY_ENABLED (default OFF; when OFF the watcher is exactly Phase 1). Additional knobs (env, same EnvironmentFile as the webhook): KICKOFF_RECOVERY_MAX_RELAUNCHES=2 (escalation guard), KICKOFF_RECOVERY_COOLDOWN=600s + KICKOFF_RECOVERY_BACKOFF=2.0 (cooldown/backoff per issue), KICKOFF_RECOVERY_MODELS (verified paid model pool; default opencode-go/deepseek-v4-pro,opencode-go/gpt-5.6-luna — model/provider variation), KICKOFF_RECOVERY_TOKEN_BUDGET + KICKOFF_RECOVERY_TOKENS_PER_RELAUNCH (per-issue token budget), KICKOFF_RECOVERY_SYSTEMIC_WINDOW + KICKOFF_RECOVERY_SYSTEMIC_STALLS=2 (systemic-correlation HALT).\n\n(2) DETECTION — keep Phase 1 heartbeat-primary + 2-consecutive debounce + LAUNCHING grace. ADD completion-edge (commit-ground-truth, playbook §6.1): non-terminal status + stale heartbeat + git branch has a [#N] commit + tmux session dead => COMPLETED, NOT STALLED (no recovery). Read .kickoff-session for the tmux name; read issue N from .crosslink/.active-issue or KICKOFF.md.\n\n(3) STALLED ACTION CHAIN (only when enabled AND all gates pass) — notify operator (Phase 1 behavior preserved) -> PRESERVE WORK (git add with kickoff-file exclusions + commit 'wip: preserve work before stall recovery [#N]'; skip clean trees; respect index.lock) -> kill tmux (tmux kill-session) -> steal stale lock best-effort (crosslink locks steal N) -> RELAUNCH fresh agent on same issue (crosslink kickoff run from repo root --issue N --model <varied> --timeout <orig> with retry-handoff description pointing to preserved branch) -> record recovery (crosslink issue comment N --kind observation) + crosslink sync. Per-issue counters (relaunch_count, last_relaunch_at, last_model, tokens_spent) live in a global 'issues' state map because each relaunch creates a NEW worktree slug; stall ledger (ts, slug, issue) powers systemic HALT. Idempotent: mark recovery_attempted_at before the chain; increment per-issue count only on successful relaunch.\n\n(4) GATES ORDER — debounce -> completion-edge -> systemic HALT (>=2 stalls in window => do NOT relaunch) -> escalation guard (>= max relaunches => STOP+notify) -> cooldown/backoff -> model variation (pool <2 => misconfig, no relaunch) -> token budget. Any gate failure: notify + record observation, no relaunch.\n\n(5) NON-STALL — COMPLETED/FAILED/CI_FAILED remain notify-only (never auto-relaunch; CI_FAILED is a code failure not a hang).\n\n(6) FAULT-INJECTION TESTS — tools/test-kickoff-notify-phase3.py: hermetic fake-bin stubs (tmux/git/crosslink log invocations to FAKE_LOG) + temp worktrees (stalled/healthy/completed/grace agents) + temp state; scenarios: recovery disabled = Phase 1 only; enabled = full chain (preserve/kill/relaunch/comment/sync invoked, model varied); escalation guard; systemic HALT; cooldown; token budget; completion edge. Run the real script with PATH prefix, assert stub logs.\n\n(7) DOCS — playbook §6.4 gains a 'Phase 3' subsection (opt-in destructive tier, gates, action chain, config knobs, two-repo sync note). systemd unit/timer comments updated. Do NOT modify crosslink fork source. Commit [#146].","created_at":"2026-08-06T06:25:53.631799139Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:W/FmB59qxxBOz+okYolAWohBwYZOvbCqD3QglEJZKDI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgY+26XBpdHSWIgw/22DR9Axtyh3tn15oNCDm0T8F+xREAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABATgY2Jo34fmjcB25oksypKkRU9ZSusV6/TTkK080HByfwG35ReYQSQiHSWp9RGJl4oX7pttz9j